"ANALYSIS ERROR: This model uses the INTEGRAL() function which is not yet
supported in CoolSolve. The model cannot be solved until integral table /
ODE support is implemented."
"Cold Storage Tank with Phase Change (Ice Storage)

A cold energy storage tank containing 120 m3 of water, coupled to a glycol
water heat exchanger. Glycol flow rate: 90 kg/s.
Heat transfer coefficient during discharge: AU = 0.5 MW/K.
Determine the available power curve during discharge, with glycol inlet T = 5 C.
Initial state: all water is ice at 0 C.
"
"Given data:"
V_res=120
M_dot=90
AU=1E6
t_su=5
c_p=3.8E3
"Energy balance of the system at a given instant:"
H_dot=M*u_dot
"(this is the differential equation to be integrated)"
M=V_res*1000
H_dot=epsilon*C_dot*(t_su-t_w)
C_dot=M_dot*c_p
epsilon=1- exp(-NTU)
NTU=AU/C_dot
"Integration:"
DELTAu=INTEGRAL(u_dot,tau, tau_1, tau_2)
DELTAu=u-u_1
u_1=u_ice_0
u_ice_0=INTENERGY(Water,T=-0.01,P=P)
p=1E5
t_w=if(u,u_ice_0,t_ice_0,0,t_melt)
t_ice_0=-0.01
t_melt=if(u,0,0,0,t_liquid)
t_liquid=u/c_liquid
c_liquid=4187
tau_1=0
tau_2=50000
x=if(u,u_ice_0,1,1,x_melt)
x_melt=if(u,0,y,0,0)
y=u/u_ice_0
$IntegralTable tau:10,  x,u,t_w,H_dot




